# Security review checklist

This file handles PII (SSN, EIN, tax-form data). Generic security
review under-prioritises the data-leak vectors that matter here.
Before suggesting a change, verify each invariant below. If a change
violates any invariant, **report which one and why**, propose the
minimal fix, and stop.

## Fast first-pass commands

Run these in the integrated terminal to triage:

```bash
rg -n 'document_text|ExtractedField' --glob '!tests/' --glob '!docs/' src/
rg -n 'set_attribute\(' src/bedrock_strands_agent/extraction/service.py src/bedrock_strands_agent/telemetry.py
rg -n 'arn:aws|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}' src/
```

Anything new from #1 outside the known-safe sites
(`service.py:extract`, `routes.py:extract`, `prompts.py`, templates,
`models.py`, `__main__.py`) deserves scrutiny. #2 should still be the
metadata-only attribute set. #3 should stay empty.

## Invariants

1. **PII in logs or span attributes.** `document_text` and
   `ExtractedField.value` carry SSN/EIN/tax data. Logs and spans are
   long-lived and seen by operators. Log only metadata (schema, model
   id, latency, counts).

2. **Error messages must not echo input.** `raise
   ExtractionError(f"... {raw}")` where `raw` could contain document
   text is a leak. Raise generic messages.

3. **New `/extract`-style routes need auth.** Auth is deferred to a
   sidecar/gateway per `docs/ROADMAP.md`. New POST routes accepting
   user input must reaffirm that assumption (comment / test note) or
   add auth inline.

4. **Span attribute names must not imply PII.** Names like
   `extraction.document_text`, `extraction.ssn`, `extraction.value`,
   `extraction.field_value` leak intent in distributed traces even
   when the value is innocent. Allowed set: `extraction.schema`,
   `extraction.schema_version`, `bedrock.model_id`,
   `extraction.document_id`, `extraction.correlation_id`,
   `extraction.latency_ms`, `extraction.field_count`,
   `extraction.warning_count`, `extraction.retry_attempt`.

5. **No new dependencies that log request bodies by default.**
   Verbose middleware, full-payload OTel instrumentors, or
   request-logger packages without redaction config are leaks.

6. **`extra={}` keys in log calls must be metadata only.** No `value`,
   `document`, `text`, or field-value keys.

7. **No hardcoded credentials, secrets, or full ARNs.** AWS access
   keys (`AKIA…`), secret keys, or `arn:aws:bedrock:...` strings
   (which embed account ids) must not be hardcoded. Model IDs like
   `us.anthropic.claude-...` are configuration and OK.

8. **`prod`-only env regressions.** When `service_env == "prod"`:
   never `STRANDS_OTEL_ENABLE_CONSOLE_EXPORT=true` (console exporter
   writes spans to stdout) and never `LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG`.

The CI semgrep rule `no-print-of-document-text` catches the
direct-format case mechanically. `extra={"foo": document_text}`
indirection is on the developer to avoid.
